id=led_hal_root
name=Notification LED daemon (AW2033)
version=4.4
versionCode=37
author=Bastet
description=Notification LED for Blackview Shark8 on ported Pixel ROM. Stock MTK lights HAL cannot flash on this hardware. A single event-driven daemon (chgd) drives the AW2033 RGB LED through the chip register node. Every event owns its own renderer (one render= line: mode=off|solid|breath|wave, color, solid current, and the chip preset breathing and traveling-wave share) in led.conf and runs it inside the chip. All effects live in one event pool with one owner at a time, chosen by the [priority] section of led.conf: an entry that loses the light keeps its state and its accrued lit time and takes the light back when the winner ends, and every kind is an ordinary ranked entry (the charge band included, it just has the lowest default rank). Notifications arrive over the standalone headless NotifyBridge app (com.bastet.notifybridge, abstract Unix socket, works on non-debuggable builds where event-log tags never fire), charge state comes from the same bridge as CHG events (BATTERY_CHANGED), no sysfs reads, no polling loops. GUI (com.bastet.ledgui) is an optional configurator.
